 return `<div class="qe-quark-result"><div><b>${quarkName[id]} · source hypercharge change ${quarkCharge[id]}</b><p class="qe-plot-caption">Atomic probe probabilities · logarithmic stem height</p><div class="qe-plot-scroll" tabindex="0" aria-label="Scrollable full local energy spectrum"><svg viewBox="0 20 840 195" role="img" aria-label="Complete local spectral measure for ${quarkName[id]}; thirteen visible energies${id==='Q'?' and twelve exact zero residues':''}. Horizontal axis: source excitation energy. Stem height uses a logarithmic probability scale."><line x1="40" x2="800" y1="180" y2="180" stroke="#405769"/>${stems}${axis}</svg></div><p class="qe-plot-caption">Source excitation energy · reference cost 4 is separate</p><p class="qe-foot">${lines.length} distinct local target energies; 13 have nonzero probe weight.${id==='Q'?' The other 12 have exactly zero atomic weight. Full interacting bins still retain possible leakage.':''} Each stem is a possible energy record, not a separate species.</p></div><div class="qe-quark-bin"><span>Strongest certified full eight-cell bin</span><strong>${interval(row.sourceEnergy)}</strong><small>source-clock energy · no GeV calibration</small><p>At least <b>${lowerPercent(row.originalStrongBinLower.display[0])}%</b> of original attempts reach this bin. Preparation failures, pump failures and outside-bin records are included.</p></div></div><details><summary>Every local line and the corresponding full-source energy bin</summary><div class="qe-table-wrap"><table class="qe-table"><thead><tr><th>Local source energy</th><th>Local probability</th><th>Full-source bin probability</th></tr></thead><tbody>${lines.map((r,i)=>`<tr><td>${interval(r.energy)}</td><td>${r.exactlyZeroLocalWeight?'0 exactly':'≈ '+((r.probability.display[0]+r.probability.display[1])/2).toExponential(5)}</td><td>${interval(row.allFullSourceBins[i].probability)}</td></tr>`).join('')}<tr><th scope="row">Pump failure</th><td>1/2 in the exact local ground</td><td>${interval(row.pumpFailure)}</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Outside all listed bins</th><td>0 in the local atomic response</td><td>${interval(row.outsideAllBins)}</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class="qe-foot">The local roots and residues are isolated algebraically. The full-source column conditions on preparation success and includes hopping and preparation error; the original-attempt rate above includes the preparation success weight. Zero atomic weight is not silently turned into a zero interacting bin. Preparation succeeds with probability at least ${lowerPercent(row.preparationSuccessLower.display[0])}%; every failed preparation remains in the complete law. The static reference remains a quantum system.</p></details>`;
